# Files allowed to declare a device protocol (GitHub issue #720 option a):
# a `protocol` whose retained region carries a direction, `tx` or `rx`.
# Such a file's `observe` lowerings assert device facts -- completion and
# quiescence -- that end device access and, for rx, let the CPU read what
# the device wrote. Those claims are trusted (TRUSTED_BASE.md), so the files
# that make them are named here and passed to the compiler as
# --device-semantics-file. A file is added by a reviewed change that says
# which observations it trusts, in its header.
